## Global API Access [​](https://docs.consentpro.com/runtime/api\#global-api-access)

### Recommended: Callback Queue [​](https://docs.consentpro.com/runtime/api\#recommended-callback-queue)

Use the callback queue to guarantee that Consent Pro is initialized before using the API. This is generally only needed if you load the script asynchronously. By default (async off), Consent Pro installs as two script tags — a config script followed by the runtime script. Place both directly in the `<head>`, in that order, without `async` or `defer`; this allows you to use the API immediately after the second (runtime) script tag.

html

```
<script>
  window.FinsweetConsentPro = window.FinsweetConsentPro || [];
  window.FinsweetConsentPro.push([\
    'consent',\
    (FinsweetConsentPro) => {\
      console.log('Consent Pro loaded:', FinsweetConsentPro.version);\
\
      const choices = FinsweetConsentPro.consents.get();\
      console.log('Current choices:', choices);\
\
      FinsweetConsentPro.elements.preferences.show();\
    },\
  ]);
</script>
```

### Direct Access [​](https://docs.consentpro.com/runtime/api\#direct-access)

After initialization, the runtime API is available at `window.FinsweetConsentPro`.

javascript

```
console.log(window.FinsweetConsentPro);
```

## Main API Object [​](https://docs.consentpro.com/runtime/api\#main-api-object)

ts

```
type FinsweetConsentPro = {
  version: string;
  config: ConsentV2SanitizedRuntimeConfiguration;
  instanceConfig: ConsentV2SanitizedRuntimeConfiguration['instances'][string];

  consents: {
    essential: boolean;
    marketing: boolean;
    analytics: boolean;
    personalization: boolean;

    get: () => ConsentChoices;
    set: (consents: ConsentChoices) => void;
    acceptAll: () => void;
    rejectAll: () => void;
    denyAll: () => void;
    renew: () => void;
  };

  elements: {
    banner: { show: () => void; hide: () => void };
    preferences: { show: () => void; hide: () => void };
    fixedPreferences: { show: () => void; hide: () => void };
  };

  push: (...args: ConsentProCallback[]) => void;
  destroy: () => void;
};
```

## Consent API [​](https://docs.consentpro.com/runtime/api\#consent-api)

### `consents.essential` [​](https://docs.consentpro.com/runtime/api\#consents-essential)

Returns the current essential consent state.

**Type:**`boolean`

### `consents.marketing` [​](https://docs.consentpro.com/runtime/api\#consents-marketing)

Returns the current marketing consent state.

**Type:**`boolean`

### `consents.analytics` [​](https://docs.consentpro.com/runtime/api\#consents-analytics)

Returns the current analytics consent state.

**Type:**`boolean`

### `consents.personalization` [​](https://docs.consentpro.com/runtime/api\#consents-personalization)

Returns the current personalization consent state.

**Type:**`boolean`

### `consents.get()` [​](https://docs.consentpro.com/runtime/api\#consents-get)

Returns all current consent choices.

**Returns:**`ConsentChoices`

javascript

```
const choices = window.FinsweetConsentPro.consents.get();
console.log(choices.analytics, choices.marketing);
```

### `consents.set(consents)` [​](https://docs.consentpro.com/runtime/api\#consents-set-consents)

Sets all consent choices at once.

**Parameters:**

- `consents` (`ConsentChoices`)

**Returns:**`void`

javascript

```
window.FinsweetConsentPro.consents.set({
  essential: true,
  analytics: true,
  marketing: false,
  personalization: false,
});
```

### `consents.acceptAll()` [​](https://docs.consentpro.com/runtime/api\#consents-acceptall)

Accepts all consent categories.

**Returns:**`void`

javascript

```
window.FinsweetConsentPro.consents.acceptAll();
```

### `consents.rejectAll()` [​](https://docs.consentpro.com/runtime/api\#consents-rejectall)

Rejects all optional consent categories.

**Returns:**`void`

javascript

```
window.FinsweetConsentPro.consents.rejectAll();
```

### `consents.denyAll()` [​](https://docs.consentpro.com/runtime/api\#consents-denyall)

Alias for `consents.rejectAll()`.

**Returns:**`void`

javascript

```
window.FinsweetConsentPro.consents.denyAll();
```

### `consents.renew()` [​](https://docs.consentpro.com/runtime/api\#consents-renew)

Resets consent to defaults and shows the banner again.

**Returns:**`void`

javascript

```
window.FinsweetConsentPro.consents.renew();
```

## Elements API [​](https://docs.consentpro.com/runtime/api\#elements-api)

### `elements.banner.show()` / `elements.banner.hide()` [​](https://docs.consentpro.com/runtime/api\#elements-banner-show-elements-banner-hide)

Shows or hides the consent banner.

javascript

```
window.FinsweetConsentPro.elements.banner.show();
window.FinsweetConsentPro.elements.banner.hide();
```

### `elements.preferences.show()` / `elements.preferences.hide()` [​](https://docs.consentpro.com/runtime/api\#elements-preferences-show-elements-preferences-hide)

Shows or hides the preferences UI.

javascript

```
window.FinsweetConsentPro.elements.preferences.show();
window.FinsweetConsentPro.elements.preferences.hide();
```

### `elements.fixedPreferences.show()` / `elements.fixedPreferences.hide()` [​](https://docs.consentpro.com/runtime/api\#elements-fixedpreferences-show-elements-fixedpreferences-hide)

Shows or hides the fixed preferences control.

javascript

```
window.FinsweetConsentPro.elements.fixedPreferences.show();
window.FinsweetConsentPro.elements.fixedPreferences.hide();
```

## Events API [​](https://docs.consentpro.com/runtime/api\#events-api)

Consent Pro emits runtime events that you can consume in two ways:

1. Through the runtime emitter API: `window.FinsweetConsentPro.on(eventName, callback)`
2. Through DOM events prefixed with `consentpro:`

The runtime dispatches DOM events with:

ts

```
document.documentElement.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent(`consentpro:${event}`, { detail }));
```

### Using `window.FinsweetConsentPro.on()` [​](https://docs.consentpro.com/runtime/api\#using-window-finsweetconsentpro-on)

javascript

```
window.FinsweetConsentPro.on('ready', () => {
  console.log('Consent Pro is ready');
});

window.FinsweetConsentPro.on('consent-updated', (detail) => {
  console.log('Consent updated', detail.choices);
});
```

### Using DOM events (`consentpro:*`) [​](https://docs.consentpro.com/runtime/api\#using-dom-events-consentpro)

javascript

```
document.documentElement.addEventListener('consentpro:banner-shown', () => {
  console.log('Banner became visible');
});

document.documentElement.addEventListener('consentpro:consent-updated', (event) => {
  console.log('Consent updated', event.detail);
});
```

### Available events [​](https://docs.consentpro.com/runtime/api\#available-events)

- `ready`
- `accept-all`
- `reject-all`
- `consent-updated`
- `banner-shown`
- `banner-hidden`
- `preferences-shown`
- `preferences-hidden`
- `fixed-preferences-shown`
- `fixed-preferences-hidden`
- `script-blocked`
- `script-unblocked`
- `iframe-blocked`
- `iframe-unblocked`
- `map-blocked`
- `map-unblocked`

### Event payloads [​](https://docs.consentpro.com/runtime/api\#event-payloads)

- `ready`, `accept-all`, `reject-all`, `banner-shown`, `banner-hidden`, `preferences-shown`, `preferences-hidden`, `fixed-preferences-shown`, `fixed-preferences-hidden`: no payload (`void`)
- `consent-updated`:

ts

```
{
  id: string;
  choices: ConsentChoices;
  previousChoices?: ConsentChoices;
  action?: ConsentAction;
  source?: ConsentSource;
  timestamp: number;
}
```

- `script-blocked` / `script-unblocked`:

ts

```
{
  src: string;
  element: HTMLScriptElement;
  categories: CookieCategory[];
}
```

- `iframe-blocked` / `iframe-unblocked`:

ts

```
{
  src: string;
  element: HTMLIFrameElement;
  categories: CookieCategory[];
}
```

- `map-blocked` / `map-unblocked`:

ts

```
{
  element: HTMLElement;
  categories: CookieCategory[];
}
```

## Lifecycle API [​](https://docs.consentpro.com/runtime/api\#lifecycle-api)

### `push(...args)` [​](https://docs.consentpro.com/runtime/api\#push-args)

Queues one or more callbacks to run after Consent Pro is initialized.

javascript

```
window.FinsweetConsentPro = window.FinsweetConsentPro || [];
window.FinsweetConsentPro.push((consent) => {
  console.log('Ready with version', consent.version);
});
```

### `destroy()` [​](https://docs.consentpro.com/runtime/api\#destroy)

Destroys Consent Pro and runs cleanup handlers.

javascript

```
window.FinsweetConsentPro.destroy();
```

